Rule 2 (integer padding: non-negative and yields positive spatial output sizes)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : tensor} |= v_1 ≥ 0 ∧ ((ndim(v_2) = 4 ∧ shape(v_2, 2) + 2 * v_1 ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 3) + 2 * v_1 ≥ 1) ∨ (ndim(v_2) = 3 ∧ shape(v_2, 1) + 2 * v_1 ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 2) + 2 * v_1 ≥ 1))
>>
Rule 3 (tuple padding must be a 4-tuple and have even length)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 4 ∧ v_1.len % 2 = 0
>>
Rule 4 (tuple padding values are all non-negative integers)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1[0] ≥ 0 ∧ v_1[1] ≥ 0 ∧ v_1[2] ≥ 0 ∧ v_1[3] ≥ 0
>>
